    "replication": {
      "analysis": "No conversion or loading defect identified within the preserved evidence. The independent backup verification and exact 255-tensor FP32 shape/dtype/value comparison, including the tied lm_head alias, pass. Native checkpoint config/generation bytes and prepared tokenizer/template hashes match the export. Native log identifies replication step 20; export loads 255/255 weights from the explicit trained export with resume disabled. Both evaluations are val_only, complete 64 rewarded cases, and produce no checkpoint files. Packages, frozen data, harness/source hashes match; the nine resolved-config differences are intended artifact/template paths, run names, checkpoint resume settings and local gateway port. Validation is configured greedy (temperature 0, do_sample=false, n=1, top_p=1, top_k=-1), with gateway val temperature 0. Training defaults at temperature 1 are not evidence of stochastic validation. Native 32/64 versus export 33/64 has one win, no losses, 63 ties and nine raw-answer differences: three changed calculator expressions, plus six changed responses following matching recorded tool arguments/results. Four extracted answers change; five are wording-only. The sole gain follows a changed calculator expression and numeric result, not placeholder extraction. The original first-match extractor remains unchanged; every recorded answer/reward was cross-checked against the preserved case receipts without rescoring. First model inputs match for all nine changed cases. BF16 numerical execution/batching or request-history differences are possible explanations, not established causes. Subsequent requests contain generated tool-call IDs; token-level/logit and in-memory loaded-weight equivalence were not recorded. Exact storage conversion does not prove deterministic generation equivalence. This bounded review supports publication with these uncertainties retained, not a claim that all loading defects are mathematically excluded.",
